upgrades are allowed when justified by the remediation." Given that `4.0.6` is presented as the parent version and it's higher than any current stable release, my working assumption is 
that this is a custom or internal version within the test environment. Therefore, I will not attempt to change or downgrade this parent version.

My primary objective is to address all High and Critical vulnerabilities, which are stemming from transitive dependencies within Spring Boot itself.

To achieve this, my strategy is to identify the latest compatible versions of these vulnerable dependencies. I plan to leverage the `maven-dependency-evidence` skill for this. The goal is
to find versions of `spring-expression`, `micrometer-core`, `tomcat-embed-core`, `spring-webmvc`, `jackson-core`, and `jackson-databind` that are either compatible with the current 
`4.0.6` Spring Boot version or can be justified for a minor/patch upgrade in relation to it.

